WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.632
The first line creates a CPU array with

00:00:03.632 --> 00:00:05.982
one zero. The next line calls

00:00:05.982 --> 00:00:08.722
cuda.to_device to copy that array to GPU

00:00:08.722 --> 00:00:09.114
memory.

00:00:12.114 --> 00:00:14.974
Numba compiles this Python kernel on the

00:00:14.974 --> 00:00:18.243
CPU. CUDA loads the compiled code onto the

00:00:18.243 --> 00:00:19.469
GPU when needed.

00:00:22.969 --> 00:00:25.707
One GPU thread runs the kernel. Its

00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:28.836
argument, out, is the array we just copied

00:00:28.836 --> 00:00:30.009
into GPU memory.

00:00:33.509 --> 00:00:36.194
Both arrays contain zero. Which array will

00:00:36.194 --> 00:00:38.112
change when this line runs?

00:00:44.612 --> 00:00:48.244
The GPU thread writes 42 to the GPU array.

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:50.666
The CPU array still holds zero.

00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:56.269
Copy to host waits for the kernel to

00:00:56.269 --> 00:00:59.197
finish. It returns the value in a new CPU

00:00:59.197 --> 00:01:00.173
array called result.
